usage: diffofdiffs [OPTIONS] patch1 patch2
       diffofdiffs [OPTIONS] --git-tree=DIR rev1 rev2
       diffofdiffs --help|--version

Compare the original changes in patch1 and patch2. Either operand may be
a single "-" to read standard input, but not both.

With --git-tree, each operand names a commit in DIR. Its patch describes
the changes from its first parent, or an empty tree if it has no parent.
For a merge commit, use PARENT..COMMIT to choose which parent's version to
compare against. PARENT must be a direct parent of COMMIT.

Empty comparison output with exit status 0 means no differences were found.

OPTIONS are:
  -U N, --unified=N       keep N context lines before and after each differing
                          block; the default is 3

  --max-column-width=N    cap each source column at N display columns (at least
                          2); the default uses up to the terminal width, or 100
                          per source column when no terminal size is available

  --tab-width=N           use N-column tab stops for terminal and HTML display;
                          N must be positive (default: 8)

  --backport-labels       label patch1 Backport and patch2 Upstream

  --git-tree=DIR          read both operands as revisions in the Git repository
                          at DIR (a working tree or a bare store); full source
                          files give a more complete comparison than the lines
                          quoted in patch files

  --color[=WHEN]          colorize the output; WHEN is 'auto' (the default),
                          'always', or 'never'

  -o FILE, --output=FILE  write to FILE instead of standard output; '-' uses
                          stdout

  --html                  write a standalone HTML report instead of text

  --highlight=MODE        highlight changes within paired lines:
                          'words': whole words, punctuation, and whitespace
                          'characters': only the differing characters
                          'none': no inline highlights; keep line colors
                          The default is 'words'. Text output needs
                          color enabled to show highlights.

  --theme=THEME           'dark' or 'light' for HTML (default: dark)

  --debug                 print parse diagnostics to standard error; the output
                          is not a stable interface and may change at any time

  --help                  print this text and exit

  --version               print the version number and exit
